WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.750
In 1968, oil was
discovered at Prudhoe Bay,

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.010
on Alaska's Arctic coast.

3
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:12.890
By 1977, a pipeline ran 800 miles south,
from Deadhorse to the port of Valdez.

4
00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.790
It has carried more than
18 billion barrels of oil.

5
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:19.650
Yet about half of it
runs above the ground.

6
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.110
Why not bury all of it?

7
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:23.710
So animals can pass underneath?

8
00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.870
In this mission, you'll follow the money:

9
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.070
oil revenue, and a savings fund
written into Alaska's constitution.

10
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.830
Then you'll ask who owns
the land and the oil,

11
00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.310
and compare Alaska with Greenland.

12
00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:41.310
Your mission: explain why about half of
the Trans-Alaska Pipeline runs above the

13
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:41.950
ground.
